  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There's a canny post asking for inside colliders, and while they don't state their use case, I suspect this is primarily being used to model skirt dynamics, and specifically to avoid legs clipping through skirts.\nI did some experiments with using plane colliders as an alternative to the use of inside colliders to model skirt dynamics. The main problem I observed with this is that, while you can use a pair of angled plane colliders to avoid bones slipping sideways past the legs, you run into problems where extending the leg out too far forwards, for example, causes the plane colliders (which extend out to infinity) to clip through the bone on the opposite side of the skirt.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WtIEIj-PJA4\nSo, I don't think we have a good solution for skirts just yet, and it would be good to get something before (or soon after) launch, as this is probably the biggest regression from dynamic bones.\nAn ideal solution for the case of skirts would be to have some kind of cross-links with collision checks - or at least a stretch constraint - between adjacent skirt bone chains. Failing that, a truncated plane constraint (one which does not stretch to infinity) would be enough to make okay skirt dynamics for the time being.",
